# The ledger of `ui/webview`: what a program whose interface is a web page in
# the system's own web view can do, one block per capability, and what Rebel
# answers. The lists are this machine's, 2026-11-22. Neither Go's standard
# library nor Python's holds a web view, and this machine holds no module of
# either that does (`go doc` finds no `github.com/webview/webview_go`, and
# `python3 -I -c "import webview"` answers `ModuleNotFoundError`), so their
# columns are `-`. Rust's is Tauri 2.12.5's, which this machine holds under
# `~/.cargo/registry`, its `Webview` and `WebviewBuilder` read from the
# crate's own `webview` module, its scheme, its commands and its events named where
# they stand; Tauri is the shape this package takes.

capability webview/make  the system's own web view, made in a window of a `ui` app
  heroes  ui/webview.webview, ui.Kind
  go      -
  rust    WebviewBuilder::new, Webview::builder, Webview::window, Webview::window_ref, Webview::label, Webview::with_webview
  python  -
  note    WebKit on macOS, WebView2 on Windows, WebKitGTK 6.0 on Linux; where the system has none the maker fails `unsupported` and names what is missing, never a browser the program carries

capability webview/place  where the web view stands and how big it is
  heroes  ui.set_fit, ui.rect_of, ui.set_visible, ui.destroy
  go      -
  rust    Webview::bounds, Webview::set_bounds, Webview::position, Webview::set_position, Webview::size, Webview::set_size, Webview::set_auto_resize, WebviewBuilder::auto_resize, Webview::show, Webview::hide, Webview::close, Webview::reparent
  python  -
  note    the web view is a widget of `ui`, laid out by its rows, columns and grids like any other

capability webview/assets  the page and its files served from the program, never from a port
  heroes  ui/webview.put_asset, ui/webview.remove_asset, ui/webview.assets_of, ui/webview.asset, ui/webview.Asset, ui/webview.ORIGIN
  go      -
  rust    tauri::Builder::register_uri_scheme_protocol, tauri::Builder::register_asynchronous_uri_scheme_protocol, WebviewBuilder::use_https_scheme
  python  -
  note    every file is an asset of the web view's own table at `app://localhost`, served through the system's hook for a scheme; no socket and no loopback server stand anywhere. Tauri answers each request by a closure of the program, which the language has no form for, so the program puts its files first and the layer answers from them

capability webview/content-types  the type each file is served with
  heroes  ui/webview.content_type_of
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    Go 1.27.4's `mime.TypeByExtension` on this machine for every extension it names, with `charset=utf-8` on every text, Python 3.15.2's `mimetypes` for `md`; and `nosniff` on every response, so a file is what its type says

capability webview/requests  what a request of the page is answered
  heroes  ui/webview.response_of, ui/webview.Response
  go      -
  rust    WebviewBuilder::on_web_resource_request
  python  -
  note    200 for GET and HEAD of a path the table holds, a folder's `index.html`, 404 otherwise, 405 for another method; `response_of` answers on the headless side what the native side serves

capability webview/policy  the content security policy every response carries
  heroes  ui/webview.set_policy, ui/webview.policy_of, ui/webview.DEFAULT_POLICY
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    Tauri writes its policy into the HTML it serves; here it is a header of every response, so no page can drop it, and the layer's own refuses a script written inside the HTML

capability webview/navigation  where the page may go
  heroes  ui/webview.navigate, ui/webview.page_of, ui/webview.allow_origin, ui/webview.allows, ui/webview.load_html
  go      -
  rust    Webview::navigate, Webview::url, Webview::reload, WebviewBuilder::on_navigation, WebviewBuilder::on_page_load, WebviewBuilder::limit_navigations_to_app_bound_domains
  python  -
  note    the app's own origin, the empty frames and the origins the program allowed; every other navigation is cancelled before it starts, and a page of an allowed origin is never heard by the bridge

capability webview/messages  texts from the page to the program and from the program to the page
  heroes  ui/webview.post, ui.Event, ui.Input
  go      -
  rust    tauri::Emitter::emit, tauri::Listener::listen, tauri::ipc::Channel, Webview::on_message
  python  -
  note    the page's `heroes.send` arrives as `ui.Event.message`, the program's `post` reaches the function the page gave `heroes.receive`; UTF-8, at most 16 MiB, no zero byte, the page's main frame of the app's own origin alone

capability webview/commands  a call of the page answered by the program
  heroes  ui/webview.parse_call, ui/webview.format_answer, ui/webview.format_refusal, ui/webview.format_event, ui/webview.Call
  go      -
  rust    tauri::Builder::invoke_handler, tauri::generate_handler, tauri::command, Webview::resolve_command_scope
  python  -
  note    `heroes.invoke(name, args)` answers a promise over a JSON framing of the two directions of texts; the program matches a call's name itself, where Tauri dispatches it to a function a macro registered

capability webview/eval  a script the program writes, run in the page
  heroes  refused: a script built from a program's text is an injection a posted text cannot be; the page gives the bridge a function and the program posts it a value
  go      -
  rust    Webview::eval, Webview::eval_with_callback, WebviewBuilder::initialization_script, WebviewBuilder::initialization_script_for_all_frames
  python  -

capability webview/storage  cookies and storage kept by the web view
  heroes  refused: the page's cookies and storage live in memory and end with the web view, so no page keeps state the program does not see; the program keeps its own
  go      -
  rust    Webview::cookies, Webview::cookies_for_url, Webview::set_cookie, Webview::delete_cookie, Webview::clear_all_browsing_data, WebviewBuilder::data_directory, WebviewBuilder::data_store_identifier, WebviewBuilder::incognito
  python  -

capability webview/permissions  what the page may ask of the machine
  heroes  refused: a new window, a download, the camera, the microphone, the location and a file chooser are refused to every page, so the page reaches nothing of the person's but what the program hands it
  go      -
  rust    WebviewBuilder::on_permission_request, WebviewBuilder::on_new_window, WebviewBuilder::on_download, WebviewBuilder::enable_clipboard_access, WebviewBuilder::disable_drag_drop_handler
  python  -

capability webview/print  the page printed, through the system's print dialog or straight to a printer
  heroes  ui/webview.print_page, ui.Event.print_chosen
  go      -
  rust    Webview::print
  python  -
  note    catalogue WV09, its printing part (the context menu and the zoom are not offered); the outcome comes through the queue as a print dialog's does (ui/print-dialogs) and holds the settings the page was printed with; macOS by WebKit's own print operation of the web view run as a sheet of its window; Windows by `ICoreWebView2_16::Print` after the print dialog where it is asked for (that dialog on its thread, as a print dialog's is), `unsupported` where the WebView2 runtime predates that interface, the outcome told once WebView2 has handed the page to the system and a print started not called back by an injected answer, its first run owed to the box, Linux by WebKitGTK 6.0's `WebKitPrintOperation`, `unsupported` with words where WebKitGTK is not installed; the headless side has no printer, so a program under test injects the choice

capability webview/devtools  the engine's developer tools
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    Webview::open_devtools, Webview::close_devtools, Webview::is_devtools_open, WebviewBuilder::devtools
  python  -
  note    off on every system until a program can ask for them in a debug build alone

capability webview/zoom  the page's zoom
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    Webview::set_zoom, WebviewBuilder::zoom_hotkeys_enabled
  python  -

dropped
  rust    WebviewBuilder::from_config, WebviewBuilder::with_environment, WebviewBuilder::with_webview_configuration, WebviewBuilder::with_related_view, WebviewBuilder::with_input_accessory_view_builder, WebviewBuilder::additional_browser_args, WebviewBuilder::browser_extensions_enabled, WebviewBuilder::extensions_path, WebviewBuilder::proxy_url, WebviewBuilder::user_agent, WebviewBuilder::scroll_bar_style, WebviewBuilder::general_autofill_enabled, WebviewBuilder::allow_link_preview, WebviewBuilder::accept_first_mouse, WebviewBuilder::focused, WebviewBuilder::disable_javascript, WebviewBuilder::transparent, WebviewBuilder::background_color, WebviewBuilder::background_throttling, WebviewBuilder::on_document_title_changed, Webview::set_background_color, Webview::set_focus, Webview::cursor_position, Webview::convert_file_src, Webview::run_on_main_thread, Webview::on_webview_event (the engine's own handles and settings, which a widget of a `ui` app never exposes; a page whose scripts are off, a browser extension, a proxy and a file URL each undo what the app's own origin keeps; the background, the focus, the cursor and printing are the window's, `ui`'s; a closure run on the main thread is what `ui.wait` makes unneeded)
